{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"},{"text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The diagram of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertex","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"typ