text","text":"| |"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"g","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"|), through a computed table of results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already found. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" fixes a variable, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" quantify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of families of sets (Minato, 1993). Its vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test elements in index order, with a low child for the sets without the element and a high child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for those with it. In place of the rule that removes a vertex with equal children, it removes one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose high child is the empty family, so an element n